        "id": 7301,
        "name": "Amnachaidh",
        "username": "Amnachaidh",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/a/ba8739/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2013-03-08T19:49:37.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I was playing my first (solo) game against Shattered Timelines, and provide the following cautionary tale.</p>\n<p>The hero team consisted of Omnitron X, The Scholar, Unity and ChronoRanger, all new characters for me.  We were fighting Le Capitan in Silver Gulch. What the Sea/Time Pirate was doing in the desert is unknown. She had - among other ongoings not pertinent to this discussion – three crew members and Maria Helena’s Revenge.  The environment had both Explosive Wagons out.  One had been dinged to 2 points, the other 5.</p>\n<p>The increased damage was really hurting my general strategy of using the Scholar to soak up as much damage as possible, since the +2 damage was walking right through his armor.  I blew up a wagon.</p>\n<p>In this situation – don’t blow up the wagon.</p>\n<p>The first explosion did six points of damage to all targets, including the second wagon. Which blew up, doing four points of damage to all targets.</p>\n<p>This was enough to destroy all 3 crew members, which did 9 points to all hero targets.</p>\n<p>By my count, all hero targets except the Scholar took 19 points of damage, incapacitating 2.  The scholar took only 6.  Still, it was enough for me to concede the game.</p>\n<p>So right now, my score is: Heroes – Zero Points, Silver Gulch - Eighteen Hundred Eighty-three points.   <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/grin.png?v=9\" title=\":grin:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":grin:\"></p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:37:33.295Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
